# Cookie behavior is a backport-critical area (NSHTTPCookieStorage on 10.9 predates SameSite and the
# public-suffix rules), so the WPT cookie suites run here rather than under mac-wk1's blanket
# `imported [ Skip ]`.
imported/w3c/web-platform-tests/cookies [ Pass ]

# 10.9 records a cookie's creation time to the whole second -- CFHTTPCookieGetCreationTime and
# CFHTTPCookieGetCreateDate both answer the same value for cookies made a millisecond apart -- so the
# tie RFC 6265bis 5.5 breaks by creation time among equal-length paths cannot be expressed here, and
# "For equal length paths, list the cookie with an earlier creation time first" fails. The rest of the
# suite's ordering, which is by path length, passes. Jonathan's call: a test failing for that reason
# stays recorded rather than chased.
imported/w3c/web-platform-tests/cookies/ordering/ordering.sub.html [ Failure ]

# Upstream skips this test on every port -- LayoutTests/TestExpectations names it [ Skip ], added by the
# same commit that imported it and its baseline -- so no bot has ever verified that baseline, and this
# port runs the test only because of the blanket un-skip above. It cannot pass anywhere: a child frame's
# parse-time postMessage is delivered to the parent AND replayed by testharness.js's getmessages handler,
# so RemoteContext.test_done runs twice per remote test while Tests.push counted it once. num_pending
# reaches zero while the local promise_test is still running, remote_done calls tests.complete(), and
# Tests.complete force-finishes the live test through cleanup_done rather than Test.done -- which leaves
# the provisional "Test timed out" that Test.step stamps in place of PASS. Measured here: every hop does
# send `complete`, and the top-level promise resolves one microtask turn after the harness emits.
imported/w3c/web-platform-tests/cookies/partitioned-cookies/partitioned-cookies-a-b-a-embed.tentative.https.html [ Skip ]

